sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py; output: docs/media/limit_cycle_turing_comparison.png; organism: Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/3aaa03d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 2171bdf8211cc376e4fec882bcd645f848050c6a4e0c6d15ce22984bb3384713; artifact_sha256: a323c621aa63149ccc29db5fba8d855d51e45cdd34cffd63205b81f1dff7e9e7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/limit_cycle_turing/dictyostelium_specimen.jpg=e2d2b739211bda97..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/limit_cycle_turing_reference.json=cc22252b314c8bb8..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/scout_manifest.json=e71deffb9f317a88...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979): the tri-molecular cubic autocatalytic scheme has a unique positive steady state (a+b, b/(a+b)^2), a Hopf curve b - a = (a+b)^3 and, beyond it, a Poincaré–Bendixson limit cycle | Turing (1952): differential diffusion destabilizes a stable reaction equilibrium in a finite wavenumber band; on a sphere the unstable modes are spherical harmonics | Martiel & Goldbeter (1987): a 3-variable receptor-desensitization model (rho_T, beta, gamma) with extracellular PDE rate k_e produces autonomous cAMP oscillations and relay | Gerisch & Hess (1974): suspended D. discoideum cells show spontaneous cAMP-controlled oscillations with a period of several minutes (~5-10 min) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on uniformly growing domains reaction-diffusion patterns undergo frequency-doubling with a dilution term -(L'/L) u; reconstructed_in_script: Exact equilibrium, Jacobian, Hopf curve, d_c(a,b), planar dispersion sigma(k^2) and its Turing band (q_-, q_+); RK4 limit-cycle ODE; 2D pseudo-spectral RD solver with 5 regimes and a 7-point d sweep; SHA-256-locked specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Hemispherical-mound RD solver with exact Laplace–Beltrami propagators, spherical-harmonic (Legendre) power spectrum, mound-radius sweep against l*(R) and hexagonal packing, critical mound radius R_min; elongating-stalk solver with ring-count kymograph (Pass 3 R1) | First-order and Michaelis–Menten PDE sinks with closed-form equilibria, analytical + numerical Hopf thresholds, Martiel–Goldbeter relay integration and k_e sweep, dimensionless pulse-shape comparison (Pass 3 R2) | Five Lean 4 theorems (Laws 1-5) mirrored by integer checks in --self-test; transfer_boundary: Mound radius R, stalk radius 0.08 and lengths 1->4 are in the dimensionless planar domain units (L = 6); they are NOT calibrated to the specimen's 32.9 px sorus diameter or stalk length, so the curved-geometry results are predictions of the model's own scaling, not specimen measurements | The Martiel–Goldbeter parameter set is the widely used Table I set; with it this implementation gives a 10.68 min period at k_e = 5.4 min^-1, above the ~7 min (5-10 min) Gerisch & Hess anchor; the discrepancy is reported, not tuned away | Schnakenberg u is identified with extracellular cAMP for the PDE sink; the 2-species model has no receptor variable, so the pulse-shape comparison with Martiel–Goldbeter is dimensionless (duty cycle, fold change, waveform r = 0.78), not a time-scale match; does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D solver of the culminant, tip-growth (non-uniform) stalk elongation, chemotactic cell movement, or that Turing rings on a stalk are an observed Dictyostelium phenotype; a digitized comparison with Martiel & Goldbeter's own time-series figures; spatial (Turing) analysis of the PDE-extended model]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(87)83275-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/253540a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.71.5.2118>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004367> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.898"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "3aaa03d" .
}

